 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Types and gain grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "BCX51 is rated -45 V collector-base and collector-emitter, BCX52 -60 V for both, BCX53 -100 V collector-base and -80 V collector-emitter. Without a suffix the gain at IC = -150 mA lies between 63 and 250; the -10 suffix narrows it to 63 to 160 and -16 to 100 to 250. Each part carries a two-letter code on the body, AL for BCX53-16."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = -2 V the gain is near 320 at 100 °C and near 230 at 25 °C at -1 mA, drifting down slowly to about 220 and 165 at -130 mA, then falling faster to about 30 to 45 at -1 A (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "With base current one tenth of the collector current, VCE(sat) is about -40 to -50 mV from -1 mA to -10 mA and climbs to about -400 mV near -900 mA (Fig.3). VBE(sat) under the same drive runs from about -370 mV (100 °C) and -420 mV (-25 °C) at -0.1 mA to about -910 and -970 mV at -1 A (Fig.4)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 1 MHz the input capacitance Cib falls from about 110 pF at -0.1 V reverse bias to about 40 pF at -10 V, and the output capacitance Cob from about 40 pF at -0.1 V to about 10 pF at -20 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-89 body is moulded in compound rated UL 94V-0, RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is level 1 to J-STD-020, with a lead-free reflow peak of 260 °C. One unit weighs 0.055 g."
  }
 ],
